ry by bonding with the spirit  tree in the navi Faith energy is only  ever borrowed as Jake reminds us in a  monologue sooner or later you have to  give it back to AWA while it's nice to  see Jake and atiri get a bit of  optimistic closure for their son's death  we still don't really understand what  they're seeing during the bond is this  just a memory or are they truly seeing  the Tam again perhaps future films will  further explore how this ancestral  connection works after absolutely  decimating Court's remaining crew and  arguably the best action sequence in  Avatar 2 nataria pulls an extreme tactic  to secure Tuck's safety quarrich emerges  with the girl held under his knife so  natiri responds in kind she grabs spider  pain and rage burning on her like an  aura and threatens to gut him if tuck  isn't released while kwarich scoffs at  first and claims that he doesn't care  about his son he quickly blanches  seemingly despite himself and lets tuck  go would natiri have killed spider in  the scene it's hard to say we're told  early on Via Jake's narration that she's  never fully trusted the kid but she  still seems to treat him with love and  respect the few times they do interact  it's possible that this was all just a  Gambit but it's also possible that  natiri wanted blood this is our home  unfortunately the way of water doesn't  give us much real character analysis  here to grab onto the film clocks in at  an absolutely bloated 192 minutes  leaving plenty of time to build up to  this moment with more Intrigue but  that's not what we get clearly James  Cameron is more interested in giving us  a sixth underwater swimming sequence  then a bit more character development  and the film sadly suffers for it even  still Zoe Saldana is so good here that  it almost doesn't matter if you thought  Avatar the way of water was done after  the whale fight or after natayam's death  or even after Tuck's rescue you'd be  wrong there's still more action mainly  in the form of 